      :start-byte 5392,
      :text
      "## Project Accounting Removal\n\nProject cost models, work-unit budgets, producer/caller debits, prospective\nreservations, cost proofs and budget-exhaustion refusals are removed as\nimplementation and admission requirements. Delete their enforcing code,\ncontracts and budget-only tests; do not raise their constants, rename them as\ngeneric bounds or require replacement accounting before useful work proceeds.\nInput node, depth, width, scalar, byte, token and form quotas whose only purpose\nis refusing otherwise well-formed input are part of this removal.\n\nPreserve independently meaningful semantics and validation: Unicode/UTF8,\ntypes, index and arity legality, target-format representability, profiles,\neffects, capabilities, authentic inputs, native class and callback rules,\nmetadata, source provenance and tamper detection. A retained numeric condition\nmust enforce one of those concrete requirements, not a work or cost allowance.\nActual host broker, heap, process-watchdog, capture and platform restrictions\nare separate from compiler accounting. External billing and account limits are\nnot changed by this project instruction.\n\nManagers independently discover and execute work toward their standing goals.\nNo task-count, failed-attempt allowance, preparation-only stage or discretionary\nper-run permission is an ordinary-development prerequisite. Coordinate actual\nconflicting writers and incompatible interfaces; the coordinator alone routes\nindependent acceptance and integrates main. Preserve historical attempts as\nhistory, and never retry, transfer or route around a denied/restricted action.\n"},
     :required-output
     "Resolve the finite retained mixed accounting clauses under the user accounting-removal instruction while preserving actual external billing, provider policy and independent semantic validation.",
     :adjudication
     {:removed
      "P10/R8 budget/cost language does not require project logical work, token/form/node, call/time/retry or human-review count allowances, producer/caller debits, cost proofs or budget-exhaustion refusals. Do not increase/rename these limits or require replacement accounting.",
      :retained
      "Actual external billing/account limits and concrete provider policy remain applicable to actual paid/provider operations. Retain observed cost/token facts only where they record external provider use or a separately required audit fact, without an internal admission/debit obligation.",
      :independent-semantics
      "Keep profile/type/effect/capability legality, exact schema and sink validation, prompt/taint/secret policy, required human review, provider identity/substitution policy, replay barriers, retention/deletion and semantic failure/cancellation/retry/idempotency/compensation behavior. Actual host timeout/watchdog/heap/capture/platform restrictions are separate.",
      :mixed-diagnostics
      "P10-BUDGET/R8-BUDGET text supplies no authority for project accounting. Existing external-policy denials keep their concrete provider/account subject and stable policy context; no diagnostic/schema rewrite or replacement diagnostic ID is proposed here.",
      :source-edit :none-canonical-owner-adjudication-only},
     :source-facet-ids nil,
     :proposed-acceptance
     {:positive
      "A semantically valid source/action with required grants, schema and provider policy is not refused solely for removed project work/token/call/time/retry accounting. A legitimate paid call remains subject to its real external spending/account policy.",
      :negative
      "Retain denial of known-over-limit actual paid provider calls before issuance, missing effects/grants/review, invalid output/sink, protected-data exposure and live calls in recorded-output replay. Removing compiler accounting cannot authorize any of these.",
      :outputs
      "A source-policy disposition binding every quoted mixed span and unchanged criterion/provider-policy dependencies; eventual source-bound accepted/rejected fixtures and typed refusal/audit records remain with existing owning tasks and are unexecuted here."},
